From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <182822903+mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:08:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Spawning: exact fast paths for the chunk being ticked,
 single-biome sections and spawn state counting

Spawn pass positions that fall inside the chunk being ticked read the start
block, structure references, block below and loaded check from that chunk
instead of looking it up again. A position at least 2 blocks from every face of
a section with a single biome gets that biome without the fiddled corner
search. createState counts by ordinal and reads the world config once.
Behaviour: identical (same random draws, same results).

